Mesa 4.0.4 SGI OpenGL Utility Library (GLU 1.3)
================================================

Repository: https://github.com/chaotic-cx/mesa-mirror.git
Tag: mesa_4_0_4
Exact commit: 61b226a4f4d29a6f7654cac22ae96b76b139bd8f
Implementation root: src/glu/sgi
Public header: include/GL/glu.h
Transport: Git over HTTPS; files imported from the pinned Git blobs.

Selection and layout
--------------------
This is the complete SGI GLU 1.3 implementation distributed with Mesa 4.0.4.
It includes utility and projection routines, image scaling and mipmaps,
quadrics, polygon tessellation, and the complete NURBS engine. Unlike the
older Mesa GLU 1.1 implementation, this selection implements the advertised
GLU 1.3 API instead of supplying partial later-version interfaces.

The upstream libutil, libtess, libnurbs and private include directories are
retained under src/. All their C, C++ and header files are selected, except
the unused top-level dummy.cc. The upstream Makefile.X11 compile list selects
16 C and 73 C++ translation units; priorityq-heap.c is included by priorityq.c
and is not compiled separately. The public header is retained under
include/GL/glu.h and copied byte-for-byte to OldenGL's public include/GL/.
SOURCE-MAP records each local path and its original upstream location.

The implementation uses C for utilities and tessellation, and C++ for NURBS.
Applications use its C ABI through <GL/glu.h>. A compatible C++ compiler and
runtime are needed to build and link GLU. The historical source has been
checked with host C89 and C++98 compilers; this does not establish a Solaris
2.6 Sun WorkShop compiler build or target hardware validation.

License
-------
The SGI sources and public header retain the SGI Free Software License B,
Version 1.1 notices supplied with this Mesa release. LICENSE.SGI-B-1.1 is
the complete license text already preserved by OldenGL's renderer import,
originally retrieved from the SPDX license-list-data repository. Individual
file notices remain authoritative. OldenGL's root LICENSE does not replace
these third-party notices. No GLU code from the separately LGPL-licensed
legacy src/glu/mesa implementation is included.

Integrity and local changes
---------------------------
UPSTREAM-SHA256 records the original SHA-256 hashes for every selected C,
C++ and header file, using paths relative to this directory. These values
remain the upstream checksums if a local correction becomes necessary.
The initial import is byte-for-byte from the exact commit above. Build
integration is maintained separately in ../../mk/glu.mk.

Local source corrections:
* src/libnurbs/internals/simplemath.h and its callers in arc.cc, arctess.cc,
  ccw.cc, patch.cc and reader.cc: rename the private REAL absolute-value
  helper from abs to glu_abs. This preserves its original arithmetic while
  avoiding a conflicting declaration of the standard C++ abs(float) overload
  supplied by current C++ library headers. It also compiles on older C++
  implementations without relying on that standard overload.
* src/libutil/project.c: use actual 16-element arrays for the perspective
  and look-at matrices, preserving their exact column-major values while
  avoiding out-of-row accesses through pointers to four-element subarrays.
* src/libnurbs/internals/mapdesc.cc: initialize every element of a NURBS
  identity matrix. sizeof on the array parameter gave only the pointer size,
  leaving most off-diagonal elements uninitialized.
* src/libnurbs/internals/trimvertpool.cc: release trim-vertex arrays with
  delete[] in both pool reset and destruction, matching their new[] allocation.
* src/libutil/mipmap.c: respect padded input rows and slices when reducing
  scalar and packed images; preserve the caller's row/image stride for the
  original base upload, use tight alignment for generated images, and restore
  the caller's pixel-store state. Regression tests cover byte and unsigned-short
  images, packed RGB565, skipped rows/pixels/images and volume mipmaps.

LOCAL-PATCHES.diff records the exact corrections against the pinned source.
UPSTREAM-SHA256 intentionally retains the pre-correction hashes.
